#question(title: [Sequences vs functions -- monotonicity and boundness])[
  For any function $f$ with domain $[0, oo)$,
   \
  we define a sequence as $a_n = f(n)$.  \
  Which of these implications is true?

  #set enum(spacing: .55em + 0.35cm)
  + IF $f$ is increasing, THEN
    $display({a_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ is
    increasing.
  + IF $display({a_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ is
    increasing, THEN $f$ is increasing.
  + IF $f$ is bounded, THEN
    $display({a_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ is bounded.
  + IF $display({a_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ is
    bounded, THEN $f$ is bounded.

  #v(1fr)
]
